--
--
Representative of the round-129 libc++-23 sweep's persistent string
failure family: `std::string s(3, 'x')` against libc++-23 headers
(preprocessed in the cxx23-gate image; 17.5k lines).  Two pinned
diagnostics: `found no match for symbol '__rep'` (basic_string's
internal union rep accessor chain, __init_internal_buffer /
~basic_string) and `offset-of of member failed to find component
'__first_padding_' ` (datasizeof.h:44, _LIBCPP_DATASIZEOF machinery --
N5008 [basic.types.general] object-representation tail padding).  The
sweep (/tmp/docker_tumbleweed3.log, 2026-09-14) counts ~28 persistent
libc++-23 failures of which the string family is the largest block;
the vector family flipped CORE in round 128.
